Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:35:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] socks, http, mixed, naive: manage users through the SSM API

The same for SOCKS, HTTP, mixed and Naive, which authenticate with a
username and password: the SSM user name is the username. Upstream these
let anyone in when they have no users; bound to the SSM API, an inbound
with no users refuses every client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: packet-boats[bot] <346322443+packet-boats[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
